    <string name="extended_intro">The app connects to this device\'s wireless debugging (like Shizuku) and saves the colors in the system settings, so they stay after the app closes and after a restart.</string>
    <string name="step_toggle_title">1. Permission to toggle debugging</string>
    <string name="step_toggle_done">Granted - wireless debugging is turned on only while the app needs it.</string>
    <string name="step_toggle_body">Recommended. Without it wireless debugging has to stay on all the time. Run once from a computer:</string>
    <string name="step_pair_title">2. Pairing with wireless debugging</string>
    <string name="step_pair_done">Paired - colors are saved in the system settings.</string>
    <string name="step_pair_a">a) Turn on wireless debugging (needs Wi-Fi).</string>
    <string name="wireless_on">On</string>
    <string name="turn_on">Turn on</string>
    <string name="step_pair_network">The first time on a network the system asks for consent - tick “Always allow on this network”.</string>
    <string name="step_pair_b">b) Open Developer options → Wireless debugging → Pair device with pairing code. Settings open on the other screen, so the code stays visible next to the app.</string>
